From ad76998e91189d0304986eb69b89d667efa3d4ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 09:48:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0055 -- wave-35 Phase 12 SDL-side audio
 brackets

SDL-side companion to engine-side nx 0131 P12 audio instrumentation for
the wave-36 PLAY5 audio cost decomposition contract
(docs/PHASE11-WAVE-36-CONTRACT.md section 8). Provides the
[p12-audio sdl n=100 ...] emit line that pairs with nx 0131's
[p12-audio n=100 midi_tick_us=...] engine-side emit, giving the wave-36
operator full cross-thread (engine main + SDL audio-thread + IRQ-5
ISR) attribution for the ~31 ms unattributed audio cost surfaced by
audio_cost_attribution_unknown.md.

The wave-35 lever-pick anchor said "rank #1: Phase 12 Pixtone-decouple"
but tree-grep confirmed Pixtone is already pre-rendered (per nx 0131
commit message section "Context"). Instrumentation-first per
reconcile_deepdive_against_tree_facts.md: measure where the audio
slice actually lives before attacking it in wave-36+.

Context. Wave-35 PLAY5 was the FIRST attempt at this instrumentation
and produced zero emit data. Per
contract_grep_targets_require_enabling_env_vars.md, the wave-35
contract specified P12_AUDIO_INSTR=1 in the BAT cell but missed
FLIP_INSTR=1 (the parent gate inherited from the engine-side audit-
flush family). Both gates are essential; wave-36 PLAY5 re-runs
with the corrected gate chain (BOTH env vars in one BAT cell).

Mechanism. 4 sub-buckets emitted per 100 PlayDevice calls (one
PlayDevice call corresponds to one SDL3-DOS audio-thread iter, i.e.
one audio chunk processed):

  audio_thread:  total wall-clock spent inside DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice
                 + DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf + DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice.
                 This is the SDL3-DOS audio backend's impl-function
                 cost; complements the wall-clock-by-bracket attribution
                 inside the chunk-processing cycle.

  ring_refill:   PlayDevice's ring-write portion alone (SDL_memcpy +
                 cursor advance + auto-resume signal). EXCLUDES the
                 silence-detect scan + SDL_Delay(10) silence-throttle
                 -- those land in audio_thread on the silence-skip
                 path.

  mix_mixer:     wall-clock between GetDeviceBuf return and PlayDevice
                 entry. This is the period during which SDL3 core's
                 SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate (SDL_audio.c:1189-1295)
                 runs its mix loop, calling SDL_GetAudioStreamData on
                 each bound stream, which fires SDL3_mixer's
                 MixerCallback -> per-track TrackGetCallback ->
                 Pixtone-chunk-pull chain. Reflects the SDL3 +
                 SDL3_mixer downmix cost that nx 0131 explicitly leaves
                 to this patch's lane.

  irq_isr:       delta of patch 0100's existing doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us
                 export across the 100-call block. Re-emitted under the
                 p12-audio sdl namespace for one-stop attribution; the
                 underlying counter is identical to what nx 0131 reports
                 via the engine-side [p10-audio ...] line.

Gating. BOTH SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FLIP_INSTR=1 AND
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_P12_AUDIO_INSTR=1 must be set (strict-"1" per
CLAUDE.md). Default OFF; opt-in only. Per
contract_grep_targets_require_enabling_env_vars.md the BAT cell that
engages the [p12-audio sdl ...] emit MUST set both env vars; wave-35
PLAY5 W35A2 emitted zero data because only the leaf var was set.
Both gates resolved at OpenDevice time; cached in
g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active (single bool); hot-path guard is a
short-circuiting ternary that avoids any SDL_GetTicksNS reads when
the gate is off.

Cycle-counter primitive. SDL_GetTicksNS via SDL3-DOS's RDTSC/PIT timer
dispatch (already used by SDL/0040 + SDL/0046 + SDL/0048 in this TU).
Off-path cost: 0 ns (no reads). On-path cost: ~6 SDL_GetTicksNS reads
per chunk = ~30 cycles RDTSC on PODP83 * 6 + accumulator adds = ~5 us
per chunk = ~0.0001 % measurement distortion against the ~31 ms
audio_cost_attribution_unknown.md baseline. Negligible.

Cadence math. Each PlayDevice call processes one chunk. At Tier-2
config (1024 frames / 22050 Hz mono), one chunk is ~46 ms wall-clock,
so 100 PlayDevice calls is ~4.6 sec wall-clock per emit. Engine-side
nx 0131 emits per 100 flips (~2.0 sec at 50 fps), so the wave-36 log
will interleave ~2 SDL emits per engine emit -- comfortable cadence
for decomp.

Bracket call sites:

  WaitDevice entry:    record _p12_wait_t0 = SDL_GetTicksNS().
  WaitDevice exit:     audio_thread += now - _p12_wait_t0. (Two return
                       paths -- shutdown bail, normal room-available;
                       both accumulate.)
  GetDeviceBuf exit:   record g_p12_sdl_t_gdb_exit_ns. (Function body
                       is trivial under SDL/0054 Shape A; we
                       approximate its wall-clock as 0 ns.)
  PlayDevice entry:    record _p12_play_t0. If g_p12_sdl_t_gdb_exit_ns
                       was set, mix_mixer += _p12_play_t0 - it;
                       clear so a missing pair (e.g., shutdown race)
                       does not accumulate stale span.
  PlayDevice silence-skip path:  audio_thread += now - _p12_play_t0;
                       counter tick + per-100 emit.
  PlayDevice ring-write entry:   record _p12_ring_t0.
  PlayDevice normal exit:       ring_refill += now - _p12_ring_t0;
                       audio_thread += now - _p12_play_t0;
                       counter tick + per-100 emit.

Per memory/sdl_pause_api_must_audit_auto_resume_gates.md the gate
state lives in a separate static bool (g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active),
not overloaded onto g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled or the new
SDL/0056 g_dos_silence_detect_enabled. Three flag families across the
audio path -- shutdown coordination, perf killswitch, instrumentation
-- stay independent, avoiding the state-flag-fragmentation footgun.

OpenDevice banner emit names BOTH env vars explicitly so log captures
let the operator grep-verify the gate chain:

  ACTIVE:  "audio: SDL/0055 P12 SDL-side audio brackets ACTIVE
            (FLIP_INSTR=1 + P12_AUDIO_INSTR=1; emits [p12-audio sdl
            n=100 ...] per 100 PlayDevice calls)"

  OFF:     "audio: SDL/0055 P12 SDL-side audio brackets OFF (set BOTH
            SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FLIP_INSTR=1 and
            SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_P12_AUDIO_INSTR=1 to engage)"

Validation:
  - Strings verified in libSDL3.a: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_P12_AUDIO_INSTR
    + SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FLIP_INSTR + emit template + both banner
    variants present.
  - Compile clean at i486 -O3.
  - Off-path semantics unchanged (default OFF): every bracket guarded
    by g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active short-circuit; no behavioral
    change when env vars unset.
  - Real-HW smoke gate: wave-36 PLAY5 BAT cell sets both env vars +
    grep [p12-audio sdl ...] emits in SDLDBG.LOG (>= 10 per block per
    contract section 7 quota).

Cross-reference:
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-36-CONTRACT.md section 8 (emit format + gate
    chain)
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-35-FINDINGS.md (the W35A2 zero-emit failure
    this patch corrects via the gate chain documented in OpenDevice
    banner)
  - patches/nxengine-evo/0131-perf-phase11-wave35-p12-audio-instrumentation.patch
    (engine-side sibling; SAME env-var SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_P12_AUDIO_INSTR
    enables both halves)
  - memory/audio_cost_attribution_unknown.md (the ~31 ms unattributed
    audio cost this patch helps decompose)
  - memory/contract_grep_targets_require_enabling_env_vars.md (the
    rule that bit wave-35 PLAY5 + drives the BOTH-gate banner here)
  - memory/sdl_pause_api_must_audit_auto_resume_gates.md (rationale
    for the separate-flag-not-overloaded-flag decision)

Per memory/sdl_ai_policy.md the patch stays workspace-local; not for
upstream.
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 223 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 222 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 44eedd70d..22a5f5864 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -66,6 +66,71 @@ static Uint8 soundblaster_silence_value = 0;
    PLAY2 control measurement to isolate SDL/0050 effect within iter. */
 static bool g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled = false;
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0055): Phase 12 SDL-side audio
+   instrumentation state. Pairs with engine-side nx 0131 brackets for
+   wave-36 PLAY5 audio cost attribution per
+   docs/PHASE11-WAVE-36-CONTRACT.md section 8.
+
+   Gates: BOTH SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FLIP_INSTR=1 AND
+   SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_P12_AUDIO_INSTR=1 must be set (strict-"1" match
+   per CLAUDE.md env-var convention). FLIP_INSTR is the parent gate
+   (shared with engine-side instrumentation); P12_AUDIO_INSTR is the
+   sub-gate (so a single SET on the engine side enables both halves).
+   Default OFF: zero hot-path cost when either env-var is unset/0/empty.
+
+   Per contract_grep_targets_require_enabling_env_vars.md: the BAT cell
+   that engages the [p12-audio sdl ...] emit must set BOTH env vars;
+   wave-35 PLAY5 W35A2 hit this exact trap by setting only the leaf var
+   and producing zero emit data. Both gates resolved at OpenDevice.
+
+   Cadence: 100 PlayDevice calls per emit block. Each PlayDevice call
+   corresponds to one SDL3-DOS audio-thread iter (one chunk processed),
+   so n=100 means "~100 audio-thread iters of accumulator wall-clock."
+   At 1024 frames / 22050 Hz mono in Tier-2 config, one chunk is
+   ~46 ms, so 100 chunks is ~4.6 sec wall-clock -- a few emits per
+   100-flip engine-side block.
+
+   Counters cover 4 sub-buckets per task #2 contract:
+     audio_thread: total wall-clock spent inside WaitDevice +
+                   GetDeviceBuf + PlayDevice per chunk (SDL3-DOS audio
+                   backend impl-funcs total cost).
+     ring_refill:  PlayDevice's ring-write portion alone (memcpy +
+                   cursor advance + auto-resume trigger; excludes the
+                   silence-detect scan).
+     mix_mixer:    wall-clock between GetDeviceBuf exit and PlayDevice
+                   entry (proxy for SDL3 core's mix loop +
+                   SDL3_mixer MixerCallback chain wall-clock; the
+                   period when SDL3 calls SDL_GetAudioStreamData on
+                   each bound stream + per-track downmix).
+     irq_isr:      delta of doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us across the
+                   block (existing patch 0100 export; re-emitted under
+                   p12-audio sdl namespace for one-stop attribution).
+
+   Cycle-counter primitive: SDL_GetTicksNS via SDL3-DOS's RDTSC/PIT
+   timer dispatch (same as the existing SDL/0040 + SDL/0046 + SDL/0048
+   timing usage in this TU). Off-path cost: 0 (cached static-bool guard
+   short-circuits at every call site). On-path cost: ~6 SDL_GetTicksNS
+   reads per audio chunk = ~30 cycles RDTSC on PODP83 + a few accumulator
+   adds = ~5 us per chunk = ~0.0001 % measurement distortion at the
+   ~31 ms audio_cost_attribution_unknown.md baseline. Negligible.
+
+   Per memory/sdl_pause_api_must_audit_auto_resume_gates.md the gate is
+   a SEPARATE flag from the silence-detect / quiescence flags above
+   (avoids state-flag fragmentation across the audio path). */
+static bool g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active = false;
+static Uint64 g_p12_sdl_audio_thread_ns = 0;
+static Uint64 g_p12_sdl_ring_refill_ns = 0;
+static Uint64 g_p12_sdl_mix_mixer_ns = 0;
+static Uint32 g_p12_sdl_playdev_calls = 0;
+/* Last GetDeviceBuf exit timestamp; consumed at next PlayDevice entry
+   to compute mix_mixer span. Reset to 0 after consumption so a missing
+   GetDeviceBuf -> PlayDevice pairing (e.g., shutdown path) does not
+   accumulate a stale span. */
+static Uint64 g_p12_sdl_t_gdb_exit_ns = 0;
+/* IRQ-5 wall-us baseline at last emit; per-block delta computed at
+   each emit via doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us - baseline. */
+static Uint32 g_p12_sdl_irq_wall_us_baseline = 0;
+
 static void ResetSoundBlasterDSP(void)
 {
     // reset the DSP.
@@ -457,6 +522,14 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
     struct SDL_PrivateAudioData *hidden = device->hidden;
     const int size = hidden->ring_size;
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0055): P12 SDL-side audio bracket
+       entry. Records timer at WaitDevice entry; the matching accumulator
+       update fires just before each return path below. Off-path cost:
+       1 cached-bool branch + 0 SDL_GetTicksNS reads when the gate is
+       inactive (ternary short-circuits the read). */
+    const Uint64 _p12_wait_t0 =
+        g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active ? SDL_GetTicksNS() : 0;
+
     for (;;) {
         /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0046): bail out early when the
            audio device is shutting down. SDL3 audio core sets
@@ -470,6 +543,10 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
            next iteration observe device->shutdown and exit cleanly,
            releasing the SDL_WaitThread join. */
         if (SDL_GetAtomicInt(&device->shutdown)) {
+            /* patch 0055: P12 bracket exit (shutdown path). */
+            if (g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active) {
+                g_p12_sdl_audio_thread_ns += SDL_GetTicksNS() - _p12_wait_t0;
+            }
             return true;
         }
 
@@ -486,6 +563,11 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_WaitDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
         // the ISR. Read the ISR's copy so we see the latest drain position.
         const int used = hidden->ring_write - isr_ring_read;
         if ((size - used) >= hidden->chunk_size) {
+            /* patch 0055: P12 bracket exit (room-available path; the
+               common case in steady-state playback). */
+            if (g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active) {
+                g_p12_sdl_audio_thread_ns += SDL_GetTicksNS() - _p12_wait_t0;
+            }
             return true; // room for at least one chunk
         }
         DOS_Yield();
@@ -519,6 +601,43 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
         }
     }
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0055): resolve P12 SDL-side audio
+       instrumentation gates once at OpenDevice time. BOTH FLIP_INSTR
+       AND P12_AUDIO_INSTR must be set to "1" (strict-"1" match) for
+       the hot-path brackets to engage. Default OFF; opt-in via env.
+       Cached at module scope; the hot-path guard is a single bool read.
+
+       Per contract_grep_targets_require_enabling_env_vars.md: BAT cells
+       MUST set both env vars; wave-35 PLAY5 emitted zero data because
+       only the leaf var was set. Boot banner emit names both vars
+       explicitly so the operator can grep-verify the gate chain. */
+    {
+        const char *flip_hint = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FLIP_INSTR");
+        const char *p12_hint = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_P12_AUDIO_INSTR");
+        const bool flip_on =
+            (flip_hint && flip_hint[0] == '1' && flip_hint[1] == 0);
+        const bool p12_on =
+            (p12_hint && p12_hint[0] == '1' && p12_hint[1] == 0);
+        g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active = flip_on && p12_on;
+        if (g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active) {
+            doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0055 P12 SDL-side audio brackets ACTIVE "
+                             "(FLIP_INSTR=1 + P12_AUDIO_INSTR=1; emits "
+                             "[p12-audio sdl n=100 ...] per 100 PlayDevice calls)");
+            /* Reset accumulators + baseline so the first emit measures
+               from this point forward, not from process start. */
+            g_p12_sdl_audio_thread_ns = 0;
+            g_p12_sdl_ring_refill_ns = 0;
+            g_p12_sdl_mix_mixer_ns = 0;
+            g_p12_sdl_playdev_calls = 0;
+            g_p12_sdl_t_gdb_exit_ns = 0;
+            g_p12_sdl_irq_wall_us_baseline = doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us;
+        } else {
+            doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0055 P12 SDL-side audio brackets OFF "
+                             "(set BOTH SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FLIP_INSTR=1 and "
+                             "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_P12_AUDIO_INSTR=1 to engage)");
+        }
+    }
+
     if (is_sb16) {
         // SB16 (DSP >= 4): 16-bit stereo signed
         device->spec.format = SDL_AUDIO_S16LE;
@@ -967,8 +1086,23 @@ static Uint8 *DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf(SDL_AudioDevice *device, int *buffer_
        in tree for documentation per `pressure_test_tidy_narratives.md`
        -- fixing-the-wrong-layer is a useful negative-result reference),
        SDL/0053 (BeginShutdown semantic preserved). */
-    (void)device;
     (void)buffer_size; /* unchanged; ring writes happen in PlayDevice */
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0055): P12 SDL-side audio bracket
+       for GetDeviceBuf. Records t_gdb_exit just before returning so the
+       next PlayDevice entry can compute the mix_mixer span across the
+       SDL3 audio core's mix loop (the period during which SDL3 calls
+       SDL_GetAudioStreamData on each bound stream, firing SDL3_mixer's
+       MixerCallback chain). Also folds the trivial GetDeviceBuf
+       wall-clock into the audio_thread accumulator. */
+    if (g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active) {
+        const Uint64 _p12_now = SDL_GetTicksNS();
+        g_p12_sdl_t_gdb_exit_ns = _p12_now;
+        /* GetDeviceBuf wall-clock is trivial under Shape A (just two
+           assignments + return), so we approximate it as 0 ns and let
+           the audio_thread bucket capture WaitDevice + PlayDevice only.
+           Future shapes that grow GetDeviceBuf can add a t0 here. */
+    }
     return device->hidden->staging_buffer;
 }
 
@@ -978,6 +1112,23 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device, const Uint8 *buf
 {
     struct SDL_PrivateAudioData *hidden = device->hidden;
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0055): P12 SDL-side audio bracket
+       for PlayDevice. Records PlayDevice entry; closes the mix_mixer
+       span (GetDeviceBuf exit -> PlayDevice entry == SDL3 core's mix
+       loop wall-clock); the matching audio_thread accumulator update
+       + per-block-emit logic fire before each return path below. */
+    const Uint64 _p12_play_t0 =
+        g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active ? SDL_GetTicksNS() : 0;
+    if (g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active && g_p12_sdl_t_gdb_exit_ns != 0) {
+        /* Close the SDL3 mix-loop span -- wall-clock from GetDeviceBuf
+           exit to PlayDevice entry. This is the period during which
+           SDL3 calls SDL_GetAudioStreamData on each bound stream,
+           which fires SDL3_mixer's MixerCallback -> per-track
+           TrackGetCallback -> Pixtone-chunk-pull chain. */
+        g_p12_sdl_mix_mixer_ns += _p12_play_t0 - g_p12_sdl_t_gdb_exit_ns;
+        g_p12_sdl_t_gdb_exit_ns = 0;
+    }
+
     /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0054, Shape A): post-mix silence
        detection + skip-ring-write throttle. Replaces the SDL/0050
        pre-mix quiescence gate that GetDeviceBuf used to implement
@@ -1061,6 +1212,34 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device, const Uint8 *buf
                                g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled true
                                so this entire block is skipped during
                                teardown). */
+            /* patch 0055: P12 bracket exit (silence-skip path). On this
+               path the silence-detect scan + SDL_Delay(10) is the
+               PlayDevice cost; no ring-refill happens. audio_thread
+               captures both the scan + the SDL_Delay throttle window
+               (which is the bulk of the wall-clock here). */
+            if (g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active) {
+                g_p12_sdl_audio_thread_ns += SDL_GetTicksNS() - _p12_play_t0;
+                /* Counter tick + per-100 emit handled at end-of-function;
+                   inline equivalent here so the silence-skip path
+                   participates in cadence too. */
+                if (++g_p12_sdl_playdev_calls >= 100) {
+                    const Uint32 _p12_irq_now = doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us;
+                    const Uint32 _p12_irq_delta =
+                        _p12_irq_now - g_p12_sdl_irq_wall_us_baseline;
+                    g_p12_sdl_irq_wall_us_baseline = _p12_irq_now;
+                    doskutsu_dbg_log(
+                        "[p12-audio sdl n=100 audio_thread=%lu ring_refill=%lu "
+                        "mix_mixer=%lu irq_isr=%lu]",
+                        (unsigned long)(g_p12_sdl_audio_thread_ns / 1000ULL),
+                        (unsigned long)(g_p12_sdl_ring_refill_ns / 1000ULL),
+                        (unsigned long)(g_p12_sdl_mix_mixer_ns / 1000ULL),
+                        (unsigned long)_p12_irq_delta);
+                    g_p12_sdl_audio_thread_ns = 0;
+                    g_p12_sdl_ring_refill_ns = 0;
+                    g_p12_sdl_mix_mixer_ns = 0;
+                    g_p12_sdl_playdev_calls = 0;
+                }
+            }
             return true;
         }
     }
@@ -1069,6 +1248,15 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device, const Uint8 *buf
        sample, direct-stream OGG, etc.) OR gate disabled (killswitch
        or shutdown coordination). Write the mixed staging buffer into
        the ring. */
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0055): P12 ring_refill bracket
+       entry. Records timer at the start of the ring-write portion;
+       matching accumulator update fires after the auto-resume signal
+       block below. ring_refill captures memcpy + cursor advance +
+       auto-resume signal cost. Off-path cost: cached-bool ternary. */
+    const Uint64 _p12_ring_t0 =
+        g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active ? SDL_GetTicksNS() : 0;
+
     const int mask = hidden->ring_size - 1;
     const int pos = hidden->ring_write & mask;
     const int first = (pos + buffer_size <= hidden->ring_size) ? buffer_size : (hidden->ring_size - pos);
@@ -1102,6 +1290,39 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device, const Uint8 *buf
         MaybeServiceIdlePauseRequests();
     }
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0055): P12 bracket exit (normal
+       ring-write path). Closes ring_refill + audio_thread spans and
+       emits the [p12-audio sdl n=100 ...] line every 100 PlayDevice
+       calls. Counter-based cadence (NOT per-flip) -- one PlayDevice
+       call == one audio-thread iter == one chunk processed; at
+       1024 frames / 22050 Hz mono this is ~46 ms wall-clock per
+       call -> emit cadence ~4.6 sec under Tier-2 config. Field units:
+       audio_thread/ring_refill/mix_mixer reported in us (ns/1000);
+       irq_isr re-emits the doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us delta which is
+       already in us from patch 0100. */
+    if (g_p12_sdl_audio_instr_active) {
+        const Uint64 _p12_now = SDL_GetTicksNS();
+        g_p12_sdl_ring_refill_ns += _p12_now - _p12_ring_t0;
+        g_p12_sdl_audio_thread_ns += _p12_now - _p12_play_t0;
+        if (++g_p12_sdl_playdev_calls >= 100) {
+            const Uint32 _p12_irq_now = doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us;
+            const Uint32 _p12_irq_delta =
+                _p12_irq_now - g_p12_sdl_irq_wall_us_baseline;
+            g_p12_sdl_irq_wall_us_baseline = _p12_irq_now;
+            doskutsu_dbg_log(
+                "[p12-audio sdl n=100 audio_thread=%lu ring_refill=%lu "
+                "mix_mixer=%lu irq_isr=%lu]",
+                (unsigned long)(g_p12_sdl_audio_thread_ns / 1000ULL),
+                (unsigned long)(g_p12_sdl_ring_refill_ns / 1000ULL),
+                (unsigned long)(g_p12_sdl_mix_mixer_ns / 1000ULL),
+                (unsigned long)_p12_irq_delta);
+            g_p12_sdl_audio_thread_ns = 0;
+            g_p12_sdl_ring_refill_ns = 0;
+            g_p12_sdl_mix_mixer_ns = 0;
+            g_p12_sdl_playdev_calls = 0;
+        }
+    }
+
     return true;
 }
 
